{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785007854,"nonce":"ATHdLLmZlDrlEW2uPvxCX1P0tWY=","title":"oauth: id_token is never validated — OIDC login trusts userinfo alone","message":"OAuthAuthenticator::authenticate (crates/scarab-server/src/oauth.rs:69-127) pulls `access_token` from the token response and calls the userinfo endpoint. It never looks at `id_token`: no signature verification against the provider JWKS, no `iss`/`aud`/`exp` check, no nonce.\n\nAcceptable for GitHub (non-OIDC OAuth2, no id_token). NOT acceptable for a real OIDC issuer (Dex/Keycloak/Google), where the id_token is the authenticated assertion and userinfo is a bearer-token-authorized lookup.\n\nFix: when the token response carries an id_token, verify it against the issuer's JWKS (discovery-fetched, cached) with iss/aud/exp/nonce checks, and prefer its verified claims for the Principal subject. Keep the userinfo path as the fallback for plain-OAuth providers like GitHub.","files":null}]}